{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The NEIKO caliper fits my recent work with bolts, rivet nuts, and drilled holes because checking dimensions helps me choose parts that fit.",
    "Its stainless construction and inch, fraction, and millimeter conversions make it a plausible upgrade to the caliper I already bought."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "My fastening and fabrication purchases do not establish that I own a 3D printer, so filament requires a need and equipment I have not shown.",
    "Different filament colors and shiny finishes do not solve my current repair and assembly needs, and a five-kilogram spool implies substantial printing demand I have not demonstrated."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in tools and making things seems to have been stretched into an assumed interest in 3D printing supplies.",
    "The repeated filament choices treat color and material variations as relevant options before establishing whether I need filament at all."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases repeatedly involve fastening, joining, cutting, and measuring, which makes practical fit and compatibility especially relevant to me.",
    "I already own a caliper, so another one appeals when its construction or measurement options offer a useful improvement, rather than simply because it is another tool."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The caliper connects well to my hands-on assembly work, but the filament recommendations assume a printing activity my history does not establish."
}"}
